      "claim": "Human absolute oral bioavailability records for structurally related peptidomimetic drugs are consistently below 20%: lopinavir poor/very low (C04, C11, C20, C24), remikiren 0.2–0.3% (C06, C21, C27), enalkiren 0.5% (C10), alvimopan 6% (C08, C09), revefenacin <3% (C05, C15, C17), cromolyn ~1% (C13, C28, C31), octreotide ~0.3–0.6% (C01, C19, C30), GHRP-6 ~0.3% (C12, C23), and SRT2104 ~14% (C02, C14).",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C11","C20","C24","C06","C21","C27","C10","C08","C09","C05","C15","C17","C13","C28","C31","C01","C19","C30","C12","C23","C02","C14"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query contains the same hydroxyethylene peptidomimetic core as lopinavir; lopinavir is repeatedly reported as having poor/very low oral bioavailability in humans (C04, C11, C20, C24). The L2 rat value of 25% for lopinavir (C46) is species-specific and does not override the consistent human low-F evidence.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C11","C20","C24","C46"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility/dissolution records for related HIV protease inhibitors show low intrinsic solubility/dissolution: lopinavir crystalline solubility ~3 µg/mL (C62, C65, C67, C72), atazanavir crystalline solubility ~1 µg/mL in bile-salt/lyso-PC (C63), darunavir plain suspension 11.2% release in 8 h (C69), and saquinavir coarse powder only 20% dissolution in 2 h (C71). These support an unfavorable absorption component for the query, though they are not direct F measurements. Formulation-dependent high dissolution (C61, C64, C66, C68) and moderate FaSSIF release for darunavir (C70) do not apply to the unformulated query and do not establish systemic F.",
      "card_ids": ["C62","C65","C67","C72","C63","C69","C71","C61","C64","C66","C68","C70"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C61","C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No fed-state-specific PK data are available for the query or an exact structural analog; transfer contexts mostly report no external condition.",
    "L4 records provide solubility/dissolution but no permeability (e.g., Caco-2/PAMPA) or direct absorption fraction for the query.",
    "The only above-threshold absolute F record (C46, lopinavir 25% in rats) is species-specific and not transferable to the human-oriented low-F evidence.",
    "Formulation-dependent dissolution improvements (C61, C64, C66, C68) do not apply to the unformulated query and do not establish systemic F."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low: transferable human absolute oral F records for structurally related peptidomimetics (lopinavir, remikiren, enalkiren, alvimopan, etc.) are all below 20%; L4 solubility/dissolution records for related HIV protease inhibitors reinforce an unfavorable absorption component, and no new evidence supports F >= 20% for the query."
}

